recordprep-summary-tools.ts.description:
Submit the completed category digest for the current document. This terminates the session on success.

Desired shape: one entry per configured category id, in the configured order. Preferred form per entry: { "id": string, "digest": {
  "text": "one synthesized digest, with detail proportional to material content",
  "evidence": [{ "text": "short verbatim source quote", "file_page": 12 }] }
A digest may contain multiple paragraphs for distinct material points; there is no word, sentence, or paragraph quota. Set digest to exactly null when the category has no material orientation-worthy content. Evidence quotes are continuous verbatim source quotations normally containing 6–12 words, usually 8–10. Choose the shortest natural phrase in that range distinguishing a substantive action, condition, reason or disputed assertion, not stock courtroom language, routine appearances, generic names/dates or boilerplate. Do not add incidental identifiers for uniqueness. Preserve negation, qualifications and attribution; copy from the declared original source page, never participant context. You see this document, not the whole record: do not claim record-wide uniqueness; repeated passages can still match more than once. Never pad, stitch fragments, insert ellipses, truncate or rewrite source wording to meet the range, or bring sentence-ending punctuation inside quotation marks. If no useful anchor exists, retain paraphrase rather than forcing a quotation. No fixed count or quote requirement in every paragraph; help locate source language, not pad or repeat digest prose. Useful out-of-range quotations remain exceptions: length checks are advisory, never a discard or another-model-pass trigger. A flattened variant (digest as a string plus a category-level evidence array) is also accepted. Python normalizes any deviation, so always submit once and never restate case text.

